==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 3 seconds<sup>90f</sup>, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*2 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 15 seconds<sup>450f</sup>, delay 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 14.93~23.87 seconds<sup>448f~716f</sup>.
**4 [[Ritual Cat (Enemy)|Ritual Cats]] spawn, delay 25.67 seconds<sup>770f</sup>.
**4 [[Ritual Cat (Enemy)|Ritual Cats]] spawn, delay 27.67 seconds<sup>830f</sup>.
**3 [[Le'noir]]s spawn, delay 25.67~27.67 seconds<sup>770f~830f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bring 3-4 cheap meatshields, [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dragons]] and a few heavy ranged attackers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] or [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Dark Emperor Catdam]]. Using [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] doesn't hurt either, while rushers like Awakened Bahamut Cat or nukers like [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tesalan Pasalan]] can help deal burst DPS to the enemies. Plus, if you're worried about the [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]], [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] is a simple choice to deal with them.

Stall as much as possible at the beginning, then face the enemy army with full force from the start, as to prevent a stack from forming on the enemy side.

